      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. One thing that's really tripping me up is the distribution of the fragments. They aren't in a neat pile; it's more like they've been scattered across a wide area of the trench floor, almost like they were kicked around or disturbed. Is it common to see such a disjointed distribution of shards even within a single stratum, or does that usually suggest something else happened to the site after the pottery was deposited?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
